{"title":"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/3674de20e2b78b5790ea714b9dcaa11af6aa2340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q,r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> that satisfy:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5de78bb2a30815698cbc0bff92b2d5ff3f0c82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q+r=26\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8160fcf6beccbf67d689256b62b8be66d9dae9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[pq + qr + pr=191\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />\nFind the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the parities, we can conclude that one of the primes must be even, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only even prime. \nWLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Then we get the equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e17495349e1a8efbc971f63d1aa49db2d8f126.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} q+r=24 \\\\ 2(q+r)+qr=191 \\end{align*}\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" />\nWe can then factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43da579f219d04c03d667268ea1efd82fde4f148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(q+r)+qr=191$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b569380ae6f210f9611b9771b26028b68ee4404b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(q+r)+qr=191\\implies 2q+2r+qr+4=191+4 \\implies (q+2)(r+2)=195\\]\" width=\"559\" height=\"18\" />\nThe only primes that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ebecc4455d2f5cba30992eda4d1cd25853975f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+r=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4916bdab3f75816d51eadfab2176af8ec7ed7a8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(13,11), (19,5), (17,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />. By testing each value, we get that only the pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e385a734686b906ab005cb8e43910c801cb37a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(13,11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies this equation. Hence the only solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4876a849f749382efc62de5e1d6867977392af5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e3ecef10f5e0017bdefaa22c0f6a634be2cafe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,13,11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and its permutations. We want to find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />, which can be evaluated as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc007fc78fc44ab39a09786f295302a5694aeb0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 13\\cdot 11=\\boxed{286}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO\">2026 Indonesia District MO </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/